<title>INDIA: India soybean, oil steady, meal firm.</title>
<headline>India soybean, oil steady, meal firm.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices remained steady in central Indian markets and plant delivery. Arrivals were around 3,000 tonnes in central Indian markets. Business volumes were dull and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices remained steady in very thin trading. The undertone was also steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were firm on overseas markets reports. Soymeal yellow was $288-290 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $116-117 per tonne in export and was 4,000 rupees per tonne in FOR condition. Business was limited and the undertone was firm.</p>
